她讲了个很棒的笑话，她说，听着，我发出的声音比那还难听呢。

307
00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.190
And then Dwight's like, we know.
然后德怀特就说，我们知道。

308
00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:42.290
This cracked me up because I feel like that moment.
这把我逗乐了，因为我感觉那一刻特别真实。

309
00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:46.870
Remember that movie, The Money Pit, where they're having so much done to their house?
还记得那部电影《钱坑》吗？他们把房子翻修得面目全非？

310
00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.630
And then she goes to open the medicine cabinet.
然后她去打开药柜。

311
00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:52.630
And when she does, there's a like construction worker on the other side.
打开的时候，里面竟然有个建筑工人在那儿。

312
00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.490
And he goes, you're out of your birth control pills.
他说，你的避孕药吃完了。

313
00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:54.770
Yeah.
是啊。

314
00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:59.210
I feel like Dwight somehow being in this clump with Pam and Jim,
我觉得德怀特以某种方式挤进了帕姆和吉姆的圈子里，

315
00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:05.750
that he's become really familiar with Pam's pregnancy in a way that you normally wouldn't.
他对帕姆怀孕这件事的了解程度，远超常人。

316
00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.610
That is such a great analogy.
这个比喻太棒了。

317
00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:08.790
I love that.
我喜欢这个比喻。

318
00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.970
We had a fan question from Carrie S.
我们收到一个来自芝加哥的粉丝凯莉·S的提问，

319
00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.150
in Chicago who said,
她说，

320
00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:15.090
I have never understood why Kathy was hired in the first place.
我一直没搞懂为什么当初要雇佣凯西。

321
00:14:15.230 --> 00:14:17.950
They lasted seven years without an office administrator.
他们没有办公室行政人员也撑了七年。

322
00:14:18.230 --> 00:14:20.930
How come they couldn't survive three months without Pam?
怎么就不能在没有帕姆的情况下撑过三个月呢？

323
00:14:21.150 --> 00:14:22.370
I had the same thought.
我也这么想过。

324
00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:24.310
I have an answer.
我有个答案。

325
00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:24.930
You do?
你有？

326
00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:25.770
Yes.
是的。

327
00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:30.470
They survived without an office administrator because Pam was receptioniSt.
他们之所以能撑过来，是因为当时帕姆是前台接待员。

328
00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.550
And she covered it all.
她把所有杂事都包揽了。

329
00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:31.970
Yes.
没错。

330
00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:32.470
Okay.
好吧。

331
00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:39.050
And now, I'm sorry, but the receptionist we currently have doesn't know how to run the fax machine.
而现在，抱歉，我们现在的接待员连传真机都不会用。

332
00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:39.630
Yes.
确实。

333
00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:40.390
Exactly.
没错。

334
00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.710
So this is why Pam needs a replacement.
所以这就是为什么帕姆需要一个替补。

335
00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:44.010
Okay.
好吧。

336
00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.150
We can't leave it to Erin.
我们不能指望艾琳。

337
00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:46.190
I'm sorry we can't.
抱歉，我们真的不能。

338
00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:46.550
All right.
好吧。

339
00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:47.350
I can buy that.
我接受这个解释。

340
00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.110
Ryan is in rare form in this episode.
瑞安在这一集里的表现真是不同寻常。

341
00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.610
I'm going to point out a few things.
我要指出几点。

342
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:57.330
But let's just start with the fact that he's lingering at front reception basically to check out Kathy.
但我们先从他一直徘徊在前台，基本上就是为了看凯西这件事说起吧。

343
00:14:57.550 --> 00:14:57.710
Yeah.
没错。

344
00:14:57.710 --> 00:15:04.650
And he wants to know if Kathy is single and Jim just sort of off the cuff, casually says, I doubt it.
他想知道凯西是不是单身，而吉姆随口就说，我怀疑不是。

345
00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.930
And Pam zero ends on that.
帕姆立刻就抓住了这一点。

346
00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.090
It's like, she's like, why, why do you doubt it?
她就像是，为什么，你为什么怀疑？

347
00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:12.150
Why would you say you doubt?
你为什么会说你怀疑？

348
00:15:12.310 --> 00:15:13.550
I mean, you were like, I doubt it.
我的意思是，你当时说的是，我怀疑不是。

349
00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.690
And he's like, hey, pump the brakes.
然后他说，嘿，慢着。

350
00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:19.430
I just thought maybe we could save her from Ryan.
我只是想也许我们能把她从瑞安手里救出来。

351
00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.650
And Pam accepts that.
帕姆接受了这一点。

352
00:15:21.870 --> 00:15:22.030
Yeah.
是啊。

353
00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:23.650
She's like, okay, fine.
她觉得，好吧，行吧。

354
00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:24.450
Done.
搞定。

355
00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:25.730
Yeah, that makes sense.
没错，这说得通。

356
00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:33.670
The next scene is Andy delivering Daryl his lunch from the fridge, hoping that he'll eat at his desk so that they can play some music.
下一个场景是安迪把从冰箱里拿出的午餐送给达里尔，希望他能在办公桌前吃，这样他们就能一起玩音乐了。

357
00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:34.150
Yeah.
是啊。

358
00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:34.910
Later.
回头见。

359
00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.430
Did you see the lunch bag?
你看到那个午餐袋了吗？

360
00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:37.790
You know I did, Ange.
你知道我看到了，安吉。

361
00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.270
Do you want to tell everyone what it said?
你要告诉大家上面写了什么吗？

362
00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:44.670
Three minutes, 55 seconds, Garrity's bag for Daryl's lunch, local grocery store in Scranton.
3分55秒，加里蒂的袋子装着达里尔的午餐，斯克兰顿当地的杂货店。

363
00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:45.970
We've talked all about it.
我们已经讨论过这一切了。

364
00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:46.170
Yeah.
是啊。

365
00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.450
We know their whole family history.
我们了解他们整个家族的历史。

366
00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:51.630
Sorry, I was curious what the lunch menu is there.
抱歉，我只是好奇那里的午餐菜单是什么。

367
00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:54.850
Well, they've got that amazing, like, deli buffet.
嗯，他们有那种很棒的熟食自助餐。

368
00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:55.710
I know.
我知道。

369
00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.130
I went on the website, and I was curious.
我上了他们的网站，我很好奇。

370
00:15:58.290 --> 00:15:59.790
You know, they do a dinner of the day.
你知道，他们每天都有当日晚餐。

371
00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:01.430
They also do a soup of the week.
他们每周还有每周例汤。

372
00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.570
Just so you guys know, this week's soup is meatball Parmesan.
顺便告诉你们，这周的例汤是帕尔马干酪肉丸汤。

373
00:16:04.970 --> 00:16:06.070
So, if you're in the area.
所以，如果你在附近的话。

374
00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.010
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

375
00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:07.470
I know.
我知道。

376
00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:11.270
We're going to swing over to Kevin's desk because, you know, he's in the band.
我们要转到凯文的办公桌那边，因为，你知道，他是乐队成员。

377
00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:15.330
And when we do that, 4 minutes, 13 seconds, you've got a Wegman's soda.
当我们这样做的时候，4分13秒，你看到了一瓶韦格曼汽水。

378
00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:17.790
I'm telling you, Phil Shea went to Scranton.
我跟你说，菲尔·谢伊去了斯克兰顿。

379
00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.350
He went to Scranton, and he came back.
他去了斯克兰顿，然后回来了。

380
00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:20.070
They're all over the place.
它们到处都是。

381
00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:22.070
Or someone sent a huge box of stuff.
或者有人寄来了一大箱东西。

382
00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:27.410
Kevin is drumming his takeout container with the drumsticks that he's eating.
凯文正用他吃饭用的鼓棒敲打着外卖盒。

383
00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:28.530
I just love that.
我太喜欢那个了。

384
00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:28.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

385
00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.170
I thought that was so funny.
我觉得那太搞笑了。

386
00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.650
The rest of the office is a buzz with chatter about Kathy.
办公室的其他人在热烈讨论凯西的事。

387
00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.490
They're all in the break room.
他们都在休息室里。

388
00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.070
No one's having lunch.
没人吃午饭。

389
00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:39.990
Everyone is having a snack.
大家都在吃零食。

390
00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.950
Some people have snacks.
有些人有零食。

391
00:16:42.170 --> 00:16:43.250
I broke it down.
我做了个分类。

392
00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:44.190
Oh, you did?
哦，你做了？

393
00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.470
I have a food breakdown.
我有一个食物分类表。

394
00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:46.430
First of all.
首先。

395
00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.030
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

396
00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:47.870
Look at my paper.
看我的纸。

397
00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:48.990
Oh.
哦。

398
00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.510
Look at us, same brain.
看看我们，心有灵犀。

399
00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.650
Food breakdown.
食物分类表。

400
00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:55.470
Well, first of all, did you notice all the Wegman's sodas?
嗯，首先，你注意到所有的韦格曼汽水了吗？

401
00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.910
There's a table of people drinking beverages.
有一桌人在喝饮料。

402
00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:58.270
Yes.
是的。

403
00:16:58.270 --> 00:16:59.870
And then there's a table of people eating.
还有一桌人在吃东西。

404
00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:00.370
Yes.
是的。

405
00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:04.530
Phyllis, Gabe, Toby, and Dwight all have a snack.
菲利斯、盖博、托比和德怀特都在吃零食。

406
00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:04.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

407
00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.850
Everyone else has a Wegman's soda.
其他人都在喝韦格曼超市的汽水。

408
00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:07.130
Yeah.
没错。

409
00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:13.610
Except for Ryan, who has a blue mug that looks exactly like our eardruMs.
除了瑞安，他拿的那个蓝色马克杯看起来跟我们的耳膜一模一样。

410
00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.220
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

411
00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:16.270
That's what I'm saying.
我就是这个意思。

412
00:17:16.270 --> 00:17:17.120
Blow out your eardruMs.
震破你的耳膜。

413
00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:19.240
I was like, wait, that looks just like our mug.
我当时心想，等等，那看起来就像我们的杯子。

414
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:20.420
That is crazy.
太疯狂了。

415
00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.520
Do you want to say what everyone was eating?
你想说说大家都在吃什么吗？

416
00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.000
Because I found the food odd.
因为我觉得那些食物很奇怪。

417
00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:26.440
Phyllis is eating giant green grapes.
菲利斯在吃巨大的青葡萄。

418
00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.320
Gabe is eating blueberries and strawberries.
盖博在吃蓝莓和草莓。

419
00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:30.460
Yeah, it looks like strawberries.
没错，看起来像是草莓。

420
00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:30.800
Bola berries.
博拉莓。

421
00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.480
Dwight has what I think is maybe some of his homemade granola.
德怀特吃的东西，我觉得可能是他自制的燕麦脆。

422
00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:35.800
That's what it looks like to me.
我也觉得是那样。

423
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.280
And does Toby have three packaged cookies?
还有托比是不是拿了三块包装好的饼干？

424
00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:38.800
Yes.
是的。

425
00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:40.460
Yes.
没错。

426
00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:43.860
There's also one more odd thing about this scene.
这个场景还有一个奇怪的地方。

427
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:46.440
We got this from Brandon R.
这是布兰登·R发给我们的，

428
00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:47.280
in Illinois.
他住在伊利诺伊州。

429
00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:52.020
Is there a reason why Dwight is reading an untitled blank book?
德怀特读一本没有标题的空白书是有什么原因吗？

430
00:17:52.580 --> 00:17:55.940
Was it because you could not get the rights to show a book?
是因为你们没能拿到展示书本的版权吗？

431
00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.440
I looked closer, and it is.
我仔细看了看，确实是这样。

432
00:17:58.440 --> 00:17:59.440
There is no cover.
没有封面。

433
00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.760
There is no title.
没有标题。

434
00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:01.840
It's blank.
它是空白的。

435
00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:03.840
I asked Steve Burgess about it.
我问过史蒂夫·伯吉斯这件事。

436
00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.140
He says he does not know why this was the case.
他说他也不知道为什么会这样。

437
00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:09.040
But it was not scripted that Dwight would be reading a book.
但剧本里并没有写德怀特要看书。

438
00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:11.240
So it might have been a last-minute idea.
所以这可能是临时起意的想法。

439
00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:13.320
And to avoid any problems with clearance,
为了避免任何版权清理方面的问题，

440
00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.400
Phil Shea probably gave him a book with no cover or title.
菲尔·谢伊可能给了他一本没有封面或标题的书。

441
00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:17.280
Hello.
你好。

442
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.940
Look at me right now.
现在看着我。

443
00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:19.800
Look at my face.
看着我的脸。

444
00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:20.160
What?
怎么了？

445
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.320
What is this face saying?
这张脸在表达什么？

446
00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.820
You deep-dived blank books?
你深入研究了空白书？

447
00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:24.300
No.
没有。

448
00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:25.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

449
00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:25.740
What is it saying?
它在表达什么？

450
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:28.080
This face is saying I have a theory.
这张脸在说，我有一个理论。

451
00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:28.900
Oh.
噢。

452
00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:30.940
Because I did so many scenes with Rain.
因为我和雷恩拍了太多对手戏了。

453
00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:33.400
The minute I watched the scene, I was like,
我一看那场戏，我就想，

454
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.940
I guarantee you Rain was like, I need a prop.
我敢保证雷恩当时肯定在想，我需要个道具。

455
00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.060
I'm telling you, the man loves a prop.
我跟你说，那家伙特别喜欢用道具。

456
00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.920
He loves a prop.
他超爱用道具。

457
00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.360
And I bet he was like, Phil, I should be reading something.
我敢打赌他当时肯定跟菲尔说，菲尔，我应该读点什么。

458
00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:44.320
Phil, I should be reading something.
菲尔，我应该读点什么。

459
00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:45.460
I should be doing something in the corner.
我应该在角落里做点什么。

460
00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.080
And Phil probably grabbed that book.
然后菲尔可能就随手抓了那本书给他。

461
00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:54.040
Well, I'll say, if you go to 5 minutes and 26 seconds, there are words in the book.
好吧，我得说，如果你看到5分26秒，书里是有字的。

462
00:18:54.300 --> 00:19:01.020
Remember in Garden Party, when Jim was reading from a literal blank book by James Trickington?
还记得在《花园派对》那一集里，吉姆读的那本詹姆斯·特里金顿写的书，其实根本就是本空白书吗？

463
00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:03.560
Okay, this is a real book.
好吧，这本是真书。

464
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.120
It just doesn't have anything on the front.
只是封面上什么都没写而已。

465
00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:07.120
I guarantee you Rain just wanted a prop.
我敢保证雷恩就是想要个道具。

466
00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:09.220
I mean, you know I used to call him Carrot Top.
我是说，你知道我以前管他叫“道具王”吗？

467
00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:09.940
Yes.
是的。

468
00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.520
Because he loved a prop.
因为他太爱用道具了。

469
00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:12.360
He loved a prop.
他超爱用道具。

470
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:16.560
Well, let's talk about what's actually being discussed in this scene now.
好了，现在我们来聊聊这场戏里到底在讨论什么。

471
00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.040
Now that we've told you what everyone's eating and reading.
既然我们已经告诉过你们大家都在吃什么、读什么了。

472
